  "english": "5. Fourth Sunday. Eve of the Fast of the Catechumens.\n12. Sunday of Saint Sarkis.\n13. Monday. The Atovmian Saints, and the Sukiasian Saints.\n14. Tuesday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n26. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Great Lent Eve [Bun Barekendan]. See also the others according to the order in the First Volume.\n7. Friday, Tone 8 [DK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n16. Sunday, Tone 2 [AZ]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\nMay\n25. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK]. Ascension of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\nJune\n4. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Eve of the Fast of Elijah.\n11. First Sunday, Tone 2 [AK/AZ]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Question [Harts] Tone 1 [AD]: \"Who came for salvation\" (Vor ekir i prkutyun).\nJuly\n23. Sunday, Tone 3 [BZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The intervening period of eating is two weeks. See in the First Volume until the Friday of the second week, and on Saturday come here.\nAugust\n5. Saturday, Tone 8 [DK]. The Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\n6. Third Sunday, Tone 2 [AZ]. Question [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who in the heavenly\" (Vor yerknayin). Eve of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\n7. Monday, Tone 2 [AK]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Question [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Ineffable essence\" (Zanchar eutyun).\n13. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The intervening period of eating is four weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n26. Saturday, Tone 5 [GZ]. Saint Thomas the Apostle. And see the others according to the order.\nSeptember\nSaturday, Tone 4 [BK]. Saints James and Simeon the Apostles. Read the Epistle and the Gospel of the Tuesday of the Fast of Saint James on this day.\nSunday, Tone 5 [GZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Question [Harts] Tone 5 [GD]: \"We glorify You\" (Paravoremk zkez). Entrance Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GD]: \"The Myrrh-bearing women\" (Yughaber), and \"Today the resurrection\" (Aysor harutyun).\nMonday, Tone 6 [GK]. Saint Andrew the Commander and his army, etc.\nTuesday, Tone 7 [DZ]. Saint Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc. Question [Harts] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Those who trust\" (Yusatsyalkn).\nThursday, Tone 1 [AD]. Saints Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and Astuadzatur the Martyr. Question [Harts] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"Holy art thou, Lord of hosts\" (Surb es ter zorutyants).\nFriday, Tone 2 [AK]. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\nSaturday, Tone 3 [BD]. The Holy Council of Nicaea of the three hundred and eighteen Patriarchs.\nSunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Question [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Ineffable\" (Ancheli). Entrance Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Christ is risen\" (Kristos yaryav). Eve of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\nMonday, Tone 5 [GD]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Question [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"The captive children\" (Mankunkn geryalk).\nSunday, Tone 3 [BZ]. Feast of the Exaltation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats]. See in the First Volume until the tenth Sunday. But look up the Questions [Harts] of the martyrs and the fasts, the Resurrection Entrance Hymns [Hambartsis], and the tone of the days in the directory [Taregirk], keeping the month.\nNovember\nSunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Tenth [Sunday]. Entrance Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"The wondrous angel\" (Sqancheli hreshtakn). Eve of the Fifty-Day Fast [Yisnakats].\nMonday, Tone 3 [BD]. Fast of the Fifty-Day Fast [Yisnakats]. Question [Harts] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"God of our fathers, who in affliction\" (Hartsan merots astvats vor i neghutyan).\nTuesday, Tone 4 [BK]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\nSaturday, Tone 8 [DK]. Saints Gregory and Nicholas the Wonderworking Patriarchs, and the other Patriarch Nicholas.",
